      ms: 4920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Say a sports league''s TV money triples in ten years, and the best coaches are no better than before. What does the talent view predict for their pay?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||It rises a lot: the same edge now wins far more money, so clubs bid more for it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So why pay a chief executive so much? Partly to make her care about the owners'' money, partly because big firms bid for a few bosses, and partly because she helps set her own pay.':
